# Rust Futures Cheatsheet

## Leaf Futures
empty()                     Create a future that never completes
ok(T) -> FutureResult       Create a resolved future from a value
err(E) -> FutureResult      Create a rejected future from an error
result(Result) -> FutureResult

## Mapping
map(F: (T) -> U) -> Future<U>
map_err(F: (E) -> U) -> Future<T, U>

## Chaining
then(F: (Result) -> Future) -> Future
and_then(F: (T) -> Future) -> Future
or_else(F: (E) -> Future) -> Future

## Joining
join(Future, Future) -> Future<(A, B)>
join3(Future, Future, Future) -> Future<(A, B, C)>
join4(...)
join5(...)
join_all(Vec<Future>) -> Future<Vec<T>>

## Selecting
select(Future, Future) -> Future  (first to complete)
select2(Future, Future) -> Future
select_all(Vec<Future>) -> Future
select_ok(Vec<Future>) -> Future  (first success)

## Utility
lazy(F: () -> Future) -> Future   Deferred creation
loop_fn(S, F: (S) -> Future) -> Future
boxed() -> BoxFuture              Type erasure

## Misc
into_stream() -> Stream
fuse() -> Fuse                    Ensure poll after completion returns NotReady
catch_unwind() -> Future          Catch panics
shared() -> Shared                Clone-able future
wait() -> Result                  Block until completion

